-- title:
--   Abs Telescope Nat
-- statement:
--   **Uniform adjacent-stage error telescopes linearly in the number of stages.**
--
--   Let `f` be a sequence of real-valued errors indexed by the natural numbers, and let `e` be an error value. For every natural number `k`, if every adjacent difference before stage `k` obeys
--
--   $$
--   \forall\ell<k,\qquad |f(\ell)-f(\ell+1)|\le e,
--   $$
--
--   then the endpoint difference obeys
--
--   $$
--   |f(0)-f(k)|\le k\,e.
--   $$
--
--   The result is the scalar triangle-inequality step that turns the per-stage move bounds into the total from-H-to-G error in `fromHToG_ofGHatFactsAndHalfSandwich`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.abs_telescope_nat`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
